        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d1b9a8ea-5893-5110-9b16-a94f8c72ad81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vinessa Shaw, Stanley Kubrick, Wes Craven, Josh Hartnett, Arthur Schnitzler, Nicole Kidman, Tom Cruise\n- Works: Ladybugs, Eyes Wide Shut, The Hills Have Eyes, 40 Days and 40 Nights, Traumnovelle\n- Topics: film roles, adaptations, filmography\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Vinessa Shaw appeared in the film \"Ladybugs.\"\n- In 1926, Arthur Schnitzler wrote the novella \"Traumnovelle\" (\"Dream Story\"), which later served as the basis for \"Eyes Wide Shut.\"\n- In 1999, Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut\" relocated the story of \"Traumnovelle\" from early 20th-century Vienna to 1990s New York City.\n- In 1999, Vinessa Shaw appeared in Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut.\"\n- In 1999, Nicole Kidman worked again with Tom Cruise on Stanley Kubrick's erotic thriller \"Eyes Wide Shut.\"\n- In \"40 Days and 40 Nights,\" Vinessa Shaw played the sadistic ex-girlfriend of Josh Hartnett's character.\n- In 2006, Vinessa Shaw appeared in the remake of Wes Craven's horror film \"The Hills Have Eyes.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
